================================================================
  CERTIFICATE TROUBLESHOOTING LAB (8 CASES: DIAGNOSE -> FIX)
================================================================

[CASE 1] Expired Certificate
  Diagnosis:
CN=expired.internal.test
error 10 at 0 depth lookup: certificate has expired
error .local/pki/troubleshoot/expired.crt: verification failed
  Fix: Re-issue certificate with valid notBefore/notAfter window ->
.local/pki/services/order-v2.crt: OK

[CASE 2] Wrong SAN (hostname mismatch)
  Diagnosis: Connecting to wrong-host.internal.test against order.internal.test cert:
curl: (60) SSL: no alternative certificate subject name matches target host name 'wrong-host.internal.test'
More details here: https://curl.se/docs/sslcerts.html

curl failed to verify the legitimacy of the server and therefore could not
establish a secure connection to it. To learn more about this situation and
how to fix it, please visit the web page mentioned above.
  Fix: Use matching SAN (DNS:order.internal.test) ->
{"service":"order-service","status":"ok","ca_version":"v2"}

[CASE 3] Incomplete Chain (missing Intermediate CA)
  Diagnosis: Verifying leaf cert against Root CA v1 WITHOUT intermediate cert:
C=PL, O=CloudAcademy, CN=order.internal.test
error 20 at 0 depth lookup: unable to get local issuer certificate
error .local/pki/services/order-v2.crt: verification failed
  Fix: Provide fullchain (leaf + intermediate CA v2) ->
.local/pki/services/order-v2.crt: OK

[CASE 4] Unknown CA (untrusted self-signed / foreign CA)
  Diagnosis: Verifying rogue cert against corporate Root CA v1:
CN=rogue.internal.test
error 18 at 0 depth lookup: self-signed certificate
error .local/pki/troubleshoot/rogue.crt: verification failed
  Fix: Replace with certificate signed by trusted Intermediate CA v2 ->
.local/pki/services/inventory-v2.crt: OK

[CASE 5] Wrong EKU (clientAuth cert used as sslserver)
  Diagnosis: Checking order-client-v2.crt (EKU=clientAuth) for sslserver purpose:
C=PL, O=CloudAcademy, CN=order-client.internal.test
error 26 at 0 depth lookup: unsuitable certificate purpose
error .local/pki/clients/order-client-v2.crt: verification failed
  Fix: Use certificate with EKU=serverAuth (order-v2.crt) ->
.local/pki/services/order-v2.crt: OK

[CASE 6] Private Key Mismatch
  Diagnosis: order-v2.crt pubkey (SHA2-256(stdin)= 95638cff0b85ebfe3e746d470e337a700a04ca4183bb85cf969b7e9b86f83ffa) != payment-v2.key pubkey (SHA2-256(stdin)= 2c706457bfec7c4d4c3159a7834cfed7cd4cd49b818afe08e8d170122d942ab3) -> MISMATCH
  Fix: Pair order-v2.crt with order-v2.key (SHA2-256(stdin)= 95638cff0b85ebfe3e746d470e337a700a04ca4183bb85cf969b7e9b86f83ffa) -> MATCH VERIFIED

[CASE 7] Protocol Mismatch (client forces TLS 1.1 against TLS 1.2/1.3 server)
  Diagnosis:
curl: (35) LibreSSL/3.3.6: error:1404B42E:SSL routines:ST_CONNECT:tlsv1 alert protocol version
  Fix: Negotiate TLSv1.2 / TLSv1.3 ->
{"service":"order-service","status":"ok","ca_version":"v2"}

[CASE 8] Wrong Trust Store (client trusts Root CA v2 instead of Root CA v1)
  Diagnosis:
curl: (60) SSL certificate problem: unable to get local issuer certificate
More details here: https://curl.se/docs/sslcerts.html

curl failed to verify the legitimacy of the server and therefore could not
establish a secure connection to it. To learn more about this situation and
how to fix it, please visit the web page mentioned above.
  Fix: Configure client with correct trust store (Root CA v1) ->
{"service":"order-service","status":"ok","ca_version":"v2"}
